of a subsequent qualifying offense as set out in subdivisions (j)(1) and (2) or any offense set out in subdivision (g)(2)(C), shall
be eligible for termination from the SOR. Upon reaching the age of twenty-five (25), the violent juvenile sexual offender may
apply for removal from the SOR by use of a form created by the TBI. The form will contain a statement, sworn to by the offender
under the penalty of perjury, that the offender has not been convicted of or adjudicated delinquent of any of the offenses set out
in subdivisions (j)(1) and (2) or any offense set out in subdivision (g)(2)(C).
