pursuant to this Code section may petition the superior court of the county where the offender resides for release from such
location tracking requirements within 30 days of the fitting. The court shall hold a hearing on the petition for release if requested
by the petitioner. The court may issue an order suspending a sexual offender from the location tracking requirements of this
Code section if the court finds by a preponderance of the evidence that the offender does not pose an immediate danger to society
due to substantial risk of perpetrating any future dangerous sexual offense. The court shall send a copy of any order suspending
an individual from the location tracking requirements of this Code section to the Department of Community Supervision.
